## ✅ Golden Rules of C Programming

No matter how basic or advanced your program gets, these fundamental rules always apply:

1. **Case Sensitivity:**
   C is strictly case-sensitive (`Main`, `MAIN`, and `main` are completely different).
2. **Main Entry Point:**
   Every executable C program must have exactly one `main()` function.
3. **Semicolons `;`:**
   Every individual statement must end with a semicolon `;`.
4. **Header Files:**
   Include required libraries at the top before using functions like `printf()`.
5. **Block Scope:**
   Code blocks are enclosed in `{ }` and must be properly matched.

